bling.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"06d814ee30d753a5fbe2bd262ba1287ba834937afeb38210e62ee7b166793a7f","compact":"3c75a106c01ab6853b047846a157263a5bcfb75cb8d539fa4f2357f4de68cf3b","nasal":"54ef57b0a3f46dda8c89aa48fdeddbf07740298a6980b944410dfa3bed0b392c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":12,"english":"Thereupon Sītā said to Lakşmaņa, the enhancer of prosperity:-:0 descendant of Raghu, I behold many inauspicious omens. My right eye and body are trembling. My mind is growing depressed. It is stricken with anxiety and I have accordingly grown restless.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-9","DUTT-7-46-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"077151bb7d5947e8a55254463bab0484b439eaa3d9cd2c054caf716b675a58cb","compact":"57159d2c6a62545f6fb50027d559e356a12f6771edc182cf5bcfe41556999b63","nasal":"9943f917f2e4c356b1b719c83e0237938b454e0022671c41ea69381cb82fa9dd"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":13,"english":"My mind is growing depressed. It is stricken with anxiety and I have accordingly grown restless. I behold the earth as void of all happiness. O you fond of brothers— has your brother met with any calamity?","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.418,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-10","DUTT-7-46-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f35743869db1176fdaaa2ff114abe9e546fa88e75297968008219e0a097bd5de","compact":"651d75479d34e036a0862a3cc22101748f8b07d7dc48c091d0a0ab381092fd9f","nasal":"651d75479d34e036a0862a3cc22101748f8b07d7dc48c091d0a0ab381092fd9f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":14,"english":"I behold the earth as void of all happiness. O you fond of brothers— has your brother met with any calamity? Are all my mothers-in-law and subjects well?","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.424,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-11","DUTT-7-46-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f8529ef2a306cff7f23614a1153fef8d8d3af186f1f11bb9126cc44eb81352db","compact":"9a40cc9aab3e11780731577b588a7156c6d64679920717c15cf10c3c3fc23039","nasal":"9a40cc9aab3e11780731577b588a7156c6d64679920717c15cf10c3c3fc23039"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":15,"english":"Are all my mothers-in-law and subjects well? Saying this Sītā, with folded hands, began to pray to gods. Hearing this Lakşmaņa bowed to her touching the ground with his crown, and though greatly sorry, said as if delighted \"All well.\"","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.451,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-12","DUTT-7-46-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"574ede93bef99c9f19b48f2b40c53d28ae18d4d47c7d34228ba322cd7ca19f54","compact":"0aa7a64dffbdc582ed88ff3e93239e0a7012ad186dc0b9ed6842aa8d411b9b85","nasal":"b46ba98077f7515c32a7890694af4d3e8d3d694a272e5198d4a8a827f4a7354a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":16,"english":"Saying this Sītā, with folded hands, began to pray to gods. Hearing this Lakşmaņa bowed to her touching the ground with his crown, and though greatly sorry, said as if delighted \"All well.\" Thereupon having arrived at the hermitage situate on the banks of Gomati Lakşmaņa spent the night there. Thereupon at dawn he rose up and asked the charioteer to get the chariot ready, saying, “Like to the powerful Mahādeva we shall hold the waters of the Bhāgirathi on our head.”","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.403,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-13","DUTT-7-46-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d218935c17aa7cfb6abb568f28cac6edf4b3af432827f53a3b54e31edf94e1d","compact":"0e0bd91bc2fa8b66e142af2f15cebd48936bb8f34d96a58e31e2fe8e3fa3993f","nasal":"ebd1a93176cfcacdfc7d27e8d031210531f7c2f47b2583fefadc12399edad532"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":17,"english":"Thereupon having arrived at the hermitage situate on the banks of Gomati Lakşmaņa spent the night there. Thereupon at dawn he rose up and asked the charioteer to get the chariot ready, saying, “Like to the powerful Mahādeva we shall hold the waters of the Bhāgirathi on our head.”","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d59621f68153bd363b79db3e9ee30f2e3f0042233e57fd3035158752135a98bd","compact":"fb06af59e0da68f0ea48fe6c42302a5aab7ca9f4f42f2d8d1a3623563a0d2264","nasal":"fb06af59e0da68f0ea48fe6c42302a5aab7ca9f4f42f2d8d1a3623563a0d2264"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":18,"english":"Thereupon having arrived at the hermitage situate on the banks of Gomati Lakşmaņa spent the night there. Thereupon at dawn he rose up and asked the charioteer to get the chariot ready, saying, “Like to the powerful Mahādeva we shall hold the waters of the Bhāgirathi on our head.”","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.724,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9028a05e6e6b8ae46c994df4a3a779b8729d6172e338289b95cdaf993128573a","compact":"83ef10b522e2925b425013ff09ae67af3a6e9025fd3b44fe7817e33a9ba09f45","nasal":"fe7456f3fe9a6250e987cadcbfd7ccf46d0f09d6db86966da9fe56980f568417"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":19,"english":"Thereupon Sumantra yoked the horses, gifted with the fleet course of the mind, to the chariot and with folded hands said to Sītā “Do you ascend the car.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.648,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"919c4c45b228882f60704cb4b7988938302b8cfafc60dfc96d8f3e0abe1ded23","compact":"7dae42d9606ef2890eb583073a88d02c01053e8390066542b9487ba95031ff01","nasal":"bf18ebb9f9f696f83f57a67568c7616162c4f411c0e054aa5a6187955ece7c86"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":20,"english":"According to the request of the intelligent charioteer, Sītā, with Lakşmaņa, ascended that excellent conveyance. In no time the daughter of Janaka, having expansive eyes, arrived at the banks of the Gangā removing all sins.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79568d8b43b1533bd94f33f7f032f3476531f7008a7ff36a6cc6370f79cc3369","compact":"91c0f6bb03563c5c64544ec89be29b6aa40bc8f59fa84313bc89834496b8df56","nasal":"6fd858425b1b944e14025377733652c396fab4fdf3cbad051855c19d846e7f79"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":21,"english":"Reaching the currents of Bhāgirathi before noon Laksmana, on beholding her, cried aloud.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"343eff5fe35fbafa7f0455db8a8a5e73fce061f249ce1a9bbb9d1688b6c65610","compact":"0f2d967a4d2d72c25deae3146411864d37b38323356267276a9b6c53779239a8","nasal":"0f2d967a4d2d72c25deae3146411864d37b38323356267276a9b6c53779239a8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":22,"english":"Thereupon beholding Lakşmaņa thus distressed, Sītā, conversant with piety, waxing are anxious said. “Why you weeping, Lakşmaņa? I have reached the banks of Jāhnavī, for which I have so long desired. So this is the time for rejoicing and do not give me pain at this time.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7045022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"867e0039300ee00744713f64f2b11b8e9ecc466c5dabd78b41198f37f0d23184","compact":"8ddebcec744d0b852b9c6ca332ce70697be51ce4385c66f558362771d1e26820","nasal":"8ddebcec744d0b852b9c6ca332ce70697be51ce4385c66f558362771d1e26820"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-45-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":45,"verse":23,"english":"Thereupon beholding Lakşmaņa thus distressed, Sītā, conversant with piety, waxing are anxious said. “Why you weeping, Lakşmaņa? I have reached the banks of Jāhnavī, for which I have so long desired. So this is the time for rejoicing and do not give me pain at this time.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-46-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskrit